The original implementation — including the provider architecture, the
chat.deepseek.com web API client (PoW solving, session lifecycle, SSE
parsing), the prompting-based tool-call protocol, the account store and
the settings panel — is the work of the upstream author. All original
upstream code remains Copyright 2026 cv-superding (Ding Li), licensed
under the Apache License 2.0.

The fork adds fixes and hardening to the image-input ("vision") path:
a self-built multipart body that survives host fetch replacement,
upload-readiness polling, rate-limit-aware retries, upload-cache
self-healing, and per-turn image scoping. These changes are documented
in README.md.

